!
! A state-reserved form of capital, as a number to count with, in Trebago
! (ninefold_model.h NF1): 1 when 4 <= form <= 7, else 0. For integers
! min(1, max(0, form - 3)) is 1 exactly when form >= 4, and
! min(1, max(0, 8 - form)) exactly when form <= 7. Trebago answers 0 for
! any other integer, where Sutra refuses one that is not a form: held.
trebago reserved
  in  form(n)
  out reserved(n)
  reserved(i) = min(1, max(0, form(i) - 3)) * min(1, max(0, 8 - form(i)))
end
